<title>JAPAN: GERMANY'S KFW LAUNCHES 40 BLN YEN SAMURAI -- NIKKO.</title>
<headline>GERMANY'S KFW LAUNCHES 40 BLN YEN SAMURAI -- NIKKO.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/U.S. dollar dual currency samurai issue was announced by lead-manager Nikko Securities on Friday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Kreditanstalt Fuer Wiederaufbau</p>
<p> AMT		 40 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    3.0 pct</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> MATURITY	  4 June 2001</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  4 September 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	August 18 to August 29</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA  Moody's Aaa</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nikko Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Nikko Trust and Banking</p>
<p>NOTES: The exchange rate was fixed at $4,553.73 per 500,000 yen.</p>
<p>---Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8584</p>
</text>
